t a politician you're  just bad in a different way if you were  more educated you're less likely to fall  for a talking point like that this is  not about elitism it's about uh uh  having gone through a process where one  learns ideally  to think things through for themselves  learns critical thinking you aren't bad  if you didn't go to college you're not  even dumb because you didn't go to  college and many people are able to  learn these things outside of college  but we're talking about tens of millions  of people here who are more likely to  fall for these empty talking points  let's continue has your life  economically financially improved under  President Trump I have I have a lot more  in my paycheck I I do have more in my  paycheck as well  my stock portfolio is doing great  maybe that's why I look at the economy  different  um I'm not where a lot of you are  financially I don't think I'm pretty  darn low income once again I have more  money in my paycheck this was one of the  biggest ruses of the Trump tax reform  and unless you know how to think about  it you get tricked like some of these  folks did the Trump tax plan included  changes to the withholding tables so  lots of people ended up with more money  in their paycheck week to week but a  smaller refund at the end of the year  but what matters is what was the total  tax that you paid I've given this  example before if I give you an extra  hundred dollars a month in your paycheck  but you get a refund when you file your  taxes that's smaller by fifteen hundred  dollars you had an extra 1200 in your  pocket during the year in your paychecks  but then you lost fifteen hundred on  your tax return you end up 300 behind  your effective tax rate has gone up  changing withholding to give people more  money week to week even though in total  they might end up with less money again  if you are uneducated you're more likely  to be tricked by that this is not a  value judgment  let's look at a little bit more of 